    "tree_id": "679061bb17957b19b34b68181b58129b8e2c99a9",
    "message": "Split trigger migrations into one statement per execute() call\n\nCI's postgres job failed applying migrations: both new trigger\nmigrations combined CREATE FUNCTION and CREATE TRIGGER into a single\nmulti-statement string passed to one schema_editor.execute() call.\npsycopg3's default extended query protocol -- unlike psycopg2's simple\nprotocol -- does not support multiple statements in a single execute().\nMigration 0002 (already proven working in CI) always issued one execute()\ncall per statement; the new migrations didn't follow that pattern. Split\neach into a CREATE FUNCTION call and a separate CREATE TRIGGER call (and\nsymmetrically for the DROP side).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "timestamp": "2026-07-23T21:41:43Z",
    "author": {
      "name": "P-Goots",
      "email": "108024002+P-Goots@users.noreply.github.com"
    },
    "committer": {
      "name": "P-Goots",
      "email": "108024002+P-Goots@users.noreply.github.com"
    }
